<BaseLayout title="2027 local elections: dates and official sources" description="England’s ordinary local election timetable is for 6 May 2027. Check council coverage, Lancashire’s reorganisation update and official voting information." breadcrumbs={[{name: "2027 elections", href: "/elections/2027/"}]}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Election dates · Sources checked 28 September 2026</p>
    <h1>When are the 2027 local elections?</h1>
    <p class="lede">The Electoral Commission publishes an England local government election timetable for <strong>Thursday 6 May 2027</strong>. This does not mean every council has an election that day.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <h2>England: scheduled ordinary polling day</h2>
    <p><a href="https://www.electoralcommission.org.uk/guidance-returning-officers-administering-local-government-elections-england/planning-election/developing-plans-election/election-timetable">The Electoral Commission’s timetable</a> is the source for 6 May. Council cycles, boundary changes and formal election notices determine which seats are contested.</p>
    <p>This is a source guide, not a complete UK ballot list. We have not verified every council, mayoralty or election in the devolved nations for 2027. By-elections can happen on other dates.</p>
    <h2>Lancashire: reorganisation paused</h2>
    <p><a href="https://burnley.gov.uk/local-government-reorganisation-in-lancashire-paused-for-review/">Burnley Council’s 7 September 2026 update</a> says Lancashire reorganisation is paused for review and May 2027 elections will use existing council boundaries. It does not confirm an election in every Lancashire authority.</p>
    <p>Our <a href="/forecasts/lancashire-unitaries/">unitary council scenarios</a> remain hypothetical. They are not a confirmed 2027 election programme.</p>
    <h2>Check your own ballot</h2>
    <p><a href="/your-area/">Find your ward and constituency</a>, then <a href="https://www.gov.uk/find-local-council">check your council’s election notices</a> for candidates, deadlines and polling arrangements. Published model assumptions cannot establish those facts.</p>
    <p><a href="/by-elections/local/">Browse the local by-elections we track</a> or <a href="/councils/">browse our council coverage</a>.</p>
  </section>
